window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/resources/hpc-v27-025-445bc7dc835922b6.json"]={sha256:"445bc7dc835922b6d57ef3772a05024840aaa25bb2db28417d3b6c3342df8bd6",value:{"sources":[{"id":"v27-case-7d2d2923d453ec72","url":"https://github.com/linux-rdma/rdma-core","title":"rdma-core verbs interfaces","titleEn":"rdma-core verbs interfaces","publisher":"linux-rdma project","scope":"查證具名案例與原理背景。課內數值、故障資料與判準為原創教學假設；請勿當作廠商規格或操作程序。","scopeEn":"Establish named case and principle context. Numbers, fault data, and criteria are original teaching assumptions, not manufacturer specifications or operating procedures."}],"media":{"courses":[{"courseId":"hpc-v27-025","videos":[],"guides":[]}]},"related":{"courses":[{"courseId":"hpc-v27-025","related":[{"id":"hpc-v27-026","referenceUrls":["https://github.com/linux-rdma/rdma-core"],"title":"HPC 封包化：payload 粒度與線上位元組","titleEn":"HPC packetization: payload granularity and wire-byte accounting","why":"用兩課的可觀察驗收條件比較模型邊界：交付 credit 帳本、狀態機、缺資源與小 buffer 反例；使用離線事件，不建立實際 RDMA 連線；請同學只使用交付件重算兩組，保留失敗案例與限制；全程使用合成檔案，不對生產系統執行故障。","whyEn":"Compare model boundaries using observable acceptance criteria: Deliver the credit ledger, lifecycle state model and separate missing-credit and small-buffer cases. Replay local events without establishing actual RDMA connections or changing registered memory on the host. Have a peer reproduce both configurations from the artifacts, retaining failed cases and limitations. Use synthetic files throughout; never inject these faults into a production system.","difference":"產生 packet_id、payload_bytes、overhead_bytes 表；每包 payload 不超上限，合計必須還原原始訊息。","differenceEn":"Generate a table of packet identifiers, payload bytes and overhead bytes. Enforce the per-packet payload limit and reconcile all payload fragments to the exact original message length.","transfer":"保留單位與邊界條件，僅轉移可證明相容的驗證方法。","transferEn":"Retain units and boundary conditions; transfer only demonstrably compatible verification methods.","practice":["在無新補充且每訊息消耗一個接收 credit 的模型中，缺口為 max(0,待發訊息數－可用 credit)；待發 120 則；可用接收 credit 名義 96、變更 128；訊息大小均符合每個接收 buffer；名義式 max(0,120-96) = 24 receive credits missing；變更式 max(0,120-128) = 0 receive credits missing。所有數值、限制與門檻為原創合成教學條件；來源支援概念與介面，不代表實機量測或設備規格。","封包數為 ceil(message_bytes/payload_limit)，總線上量為訊息量加封包數乘 overhead；最後一包可不滿載；訊息 1048576 B，每包額外 64 B；payload 上限由 4096 改為 1024 B，無重傳與填補；名義式 1048576+ceil(1048576/4096)*64 = 1064960 modeled wire B；變更式 1048576+ceil(1048576/1024)*64 = 1114112 modeled wire B。所有數值、限制與門檻為原創合成教學條件；來源支援概念與介面，不代表實機量測或設備規格。","比較兩個模型的輸入、誤差與驗收條件，記錄不能沿用的假設。"],"practiceEn":["With no replenishment and one receive credit consumed per message, deficit is the positive difference between queued sends and available receive credits. This deliberately simplified model is not a full verbs state machine. Queue 120 messages. Available receive credits change from 96 to 128, and every message fits its receive buffer. No credits are replenished during the modeled burst. Nominal max(0,120-96) = 24 receive credits missing; changed max(0,120-128) = 0 receive credits missing. Every numeric input, limit and threshold is an original synthetic teaching condition. References establish concepts and interfaces, not measured machine results or equipment specifications.","Packet count is the ceiling of message bytes divided by payload limit. Modeled wire bytes equal message bytes plus packet count times fixed overhead; the final packet may carry less payload. Send a 1048576-byte message with a synthetic 64-byte overhead per packet. Payload limit changes from 4096 to 1024 bytes, excluding retransmissions, padding and other unmodeled link framing. Nominal 1048576+ceil(1048576/4096)*64 = 1064960 modeled wire B; changed 1048576+ceil(1048576/1024)*64 = 1114112 modeled wire B. Every numeric input, limit and threshold is an original synthetic teaching condition. References establish concepts and interfaces, not measured machine results or equipment specifications.","Compare inputs, errors, and criteria; document assumptions that cannot be transferred."]},{"id":"hpc-v27-035","referenceUrls":["https://docs.daos.io/master/overview/transaction/"],"title":"DAOS transaction：衝突重試與餘額不變量","titleEn":"DAOS transactions: conflict retries and balance invariants","why":"用兩課的可觀察驗收條件比較模型邊界：交付 credit 帳本、狀態機、缺資源與小 buffer 反例；使用離線事件，不建立實際 RDMA 連線；請同學只使用交付件重算兩組，保留失敗案例與限制；全程使用合成檔案，不對生產系統執行故障。","whyEn":"Compare model boundaries using observable acceptance criteria: Deliver the credit ledger, lifecycle state model and separate missing-credit and small-buffer cases. Replay local events without establishing actual RDMA connections or changing registered memory on the host. Have a peer reproduce both configurations from the artifacts, retaining failed cases and limitations. Use synthetic files throughout; never inject these faults into a production system.","difference":"事件表包含 transaction_id、read_version、requested_debit、commit_status 與 balance_after；另保留已完成冪等鍵集合。","differenceEn":"Record transaction identity, read version, requested debit, commit status and balance after each event. Maintain a separate set of completed idempotency keys so retried delivery cannot apply one debit twice.","transfer":"保留單位與邊界條件，僅轉移可證明相容的驗證方法。","transferEn":"Retain units and boundary conditions; transfer only demonstrably compatible verification methods.","practice":["在無新補充且每訊息消耗一個接收 credit 的模型中，缺口為 max(0,待發訊息數－可用 credit)；待發 120 則；可用接收 credit 名義 96、變更 128；訊息大小均符合每個接收 buffer；名義式 max(0,120-96) = 24 receive credits missing；變更式 max(0,120-128) = 0 receive credits missing。所有數值、限制與門檻為原創合成教學條件；來源支援概念與介面，不代表實機量測或設備規格。","帳本規則為餘額不可負，交易需基於當前版本提交；衝突後須重讀再判斷，不可直接重送舊計算結果；初始 100 單位；第一交易扣 60。名義第二交易也要求 60，應拒絕；變更第二要求 30，重讀後可提交；名義式 100-60 = 40 balance units；變更式 100-60-30 = 10 balance units。所有數值、限制與門檻為原創合成教學條件；來源支援概念與介面，不代表實機量測或設備規格。","比較兩個模型的輸入、誤差與驗收條件，記錄不能沿用的假設。"],"practiceEn":["With no replenishment and one receive credit consumed per message, deficit is the positive difference between queued sends and available receive credits. This deliberately simplified model is not a full verbs state machine. Queue 120 messages. Available receive credits change from 96 to 128, and every message fits its receive buffer. No credits are replenished during the modeled burst. Nominal max(0,120-96) = 24 receive credits missing; changed max(0,120-128) = 0 receive credits missing. Every numeric input, limit and threshold is an original synthetic teaching condition. References establish concepts and interfaces, not measured machine results or equipment specifications.","Require nonnegative balance and submission against the current version. After conflict, reread and reevaluate the business rule rather than resubmitting a value calculated from a stale snapshot. Start with 100 units and commit a first debit of 60. A second debit requests 60 nominally and must be rejected after reread; changing that request to 30 allows a valid subsequent commit. Nominal 100-60 = 40 balance units; changed 100-60-30 = 10 balance units. Every numeric input, limit and threshold is an original synthetic teaching condition. References establish concepts and interfaces, not measured machine results or equipment specifications.","Compare inputs, errors, and criteria; document assumptions that cannot be transferred."]}],"references":[{"id":"v27-case-7d2d2923d453ec72","url":"https://github.com/linux-rdma/rdma-core","title":"rdma-core verbs interfaces","titleEn":"rdma-core verbs interfaces","publisher":"linux-rdma project","scope":"查證具名案例與原理背景。課內數值、故障資料與判準為原創教學假設；請勿當作廠商規格或操作程序。","scopeEn":"Establish named case and principle context. Numbers, fault data, and criteria are original teaching assumptions, not manufacturer specifications or operating procedures."},{"id":"v27-case-c359e652f7fedc4a","url":"https://docs.daos.io/master/overview/transaction/","title":"DAOS transaction model","titleEn":"DAOS transaction model","publisher":"DAOS project","scope":"查證具名案例與原理背景。課內數值、故障資料與判準為原創教學假設；請勿當作廠商規格或操作程序。","scopeEn":"Establish named case and principle context. Numbers, fault data, and criteria are original teaching assumptions, not manufacturer specifications or operating procedures."}],"overview":"比較相鄰案例與另一組案例的模型、可量測結果及可轉移的驗證方法。","overviewEn":"Compare neighboring and cross-group cases by model, measurable outcome, and transferable verification method."}]},"places":{"courses":[]},"vendors":{"courses":[],"vendors":[]}}};
